    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195-a3">

                <pb facs="0315" n="217" xml:id="pg217"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Prince Ching and Earl Li
                        Hung-chang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellency</hi>: I have the
                    honor to acknowledge the receipt of the note of your highness and your
                    excellency transmitting a copy of a proposed convention by your highness and
                    your excellency suggesting certain terms as a basis for a settlement of the
                    recent troubles which made it necessary for foreign powers to bring troops into
                    China.</p>
                <p>I have, as you request, telegraphed the convention to my Government, and shall
                    soon be ready to discuss it with you.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of the occasion to assure your highness and your excellency of my
                    highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
